{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>YHWH shall reign forever and ever. For the horse of Pharaoh.</b> One may explain the word ״כִּי״ [for]: because Pharaoh disputed the kingship of Shaddai and said ״מִי ה׳״ (Exodus 5:2), and had the Holy One, blessed be He, not executed judgments upon Pharaoh, there would be reason to fear that even in future generations rebellious children would arise and deny His blessed kingship. But now that judgment has been executed upon Pharaoh in writing, no longer will there be any who dispute or cast doubt upon the kingship of Shaddai, blessed be He, and YHWH shall reign forever and ever — for all the world will see that the horse of Pharaoh came with his chariots and with his horsemen into the sea, etc.; and from then on fear will mount upon their heads to fling words heavenward."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:20:34.566589841Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}